WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:08.200
For over 70 years, NASA Ames Research Center has been shaping the science of flight.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:16.050
From wings that enable modern commercial aircraft to spacecraft that return our astronauts safely to Earth,

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:23.380
Ames has the world-class expertise and facilities to enable a broad spectrum of aeronautics research.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.540
Located in the heart of Silicon Valley, NASA Ames is able to leverage the capabilities

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:39.220
of nearby world-renowned companies and universities.

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:45.590
For 50 years and counting, our wind tunnels have been used in the development of nearly

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:48.630
every U.S. commercial and military aircraft.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:55.240
The ArcJet simulates the heating of atmospheric entry, enabling researchers to develop thermal

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:59.740
protection systems for every NASA space transportation and planetary

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.240
program. AIMS flight simulators can model a wide range of commercial, military, and

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:13.230
space vehicles. This allows our researchers to develop and test advanced flight deck displays

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:20.210
and next-generation intelligent flight control systems. AIMS is pushing the envelope with

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:26.640
revolutionary concepts for air traffic optimization. Our advanced air traffic modeling and simulation

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.840
capabilities are critical for developing the next generation.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:37.070
air transportation system. Our supercomputing capability brings state-of-the-art data analysis

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:44.590
and high-fidelity data visualization to research partners across the globe. We are investigating

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:50.810
sustainable fuel alternatives and developing new aircraft and operational concepts to make

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:58.080
air transportation more environmentally responsible. The visionary scientists and researchers at

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.980
aims are constantly innovating.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.200
to enable the next leap forward.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.840
Whether we travel in the Earth's atmosphere or through it to another world,

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:15.750
NASA Ames Research Center will continue to shape the aircraft and spacecraft of the 21st century.
